ID: vr-59
Title: Original Verona desktop and browser identity

Status: DONE
Milestone: Post-M1 visual identity
Dependencies: vr-13, vr-45

Purpose:
  Give Verona an original face-mesh logo, native window/taskbar icon, browser
  favicons and visible README branding without repackaging the Electron runtime.

Tasks:
  Create original artwork and reproducible size/ICO derivatives.
  Update native BrowserWindow and all three supported web entrypoints.
  Verify actual asset responses, native icon and README presentation.
  Coordinate an authorized current-head restart after the complete candidate.

Acceptance criteria:
  Electron window and taskbar use the Verona icon, not default Electron artwork.
  Manager, Claire and native MPFB pages serve their declared local favicons.
  README includes the actual same logo without replacing its talking hero.
  No new network dependency, installer, retired character or sibling app change.

Completion evidence:
  Preserved docs/branding/verona-master.png and reproducible PNG/ICO generator.
    Electron BrowserWindow receives the ICO and Windows Zanark.Verona identity.
    Manager, Claire and native MPFB use explicit guarded branding routes.
  Actual guarded HTTP and native icon/window qualification pass; ICO decodes
    at 256px, favicon at 32px. README logo/hero and narrow/wide GFM layout pass.
  This chat's explicitly authorized replacement head loads current branding;
    its prior voice/appearance settings remain. Shared manager not restarted.
    Source-window branding is implemented; independent taskbar visual approval
    and changing the downloaded Electron executable/installer are not claimed.

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Owner explicitly requests original logo, app/favicon/README
    integration and permits closing heads when needed to apply the updates.
  2026-11-21 - Completed artwork/integration, native and browser qualification,
    README display and the explicitly requested owned-head replacement.
